cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Value-Field Theory (VFT)"
message: "If you use this theory or repository, please cite this repository."
authors:
  - family-names: "Nuno"
    given-names: "T."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >
  Value-Field Theory (VFT) is a structural framework for describing how
  resource states K and expectation structures P form an observable value field,
  how actions transform resource states, and how realized changes Delta K relate
  to expected changes. The framework separates expectation stock P from expected
  flow E[Delta K], and treats preference and rationality differences as differences
  in the structure and magnitude of P rather than as independent latent variables.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuno929/vf-model"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
keywords:
  - value-field theory
  - resource dynamics
  - expectation field
  - expectation stock
  - nominal-real structure
  - social dynamics
